        "title": "Turkish Air Force AS532 helicopter crashes on training flight, killing all five aboard",
        "summary": "A Turkish Air Force AS532 helicopter crashed in northwestern Turkey on November 24 during a training flight, killing all five soldiers aboard. The cause of the crash is not yet known.",
        "body": [
          "A Turkish Air Force helicopter crashed in northwestern Turkey on November 24 during a training flight, killing all five soldiers on board, according to the Turkish Defense Ministry. The helicopter had taken off in Eskisehir Province before coming down, and search and rescue teams found the wreckage of an AS532 helicopter at the scene. The ministry confirmed that all five soldiers aboard were killed, and the cause of the crash is not yet known.",
          "The crash was the second Turkish military helicopter accident in about two weeks. On November 12, an S-70 military helicopter crashed in Malatya Province in eastern Turkey, killing all four soldiers on board."
        ]
      },
